cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use haic-libs in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  below, and cite the HAIC evaluation framework it implements (see references).
type: software
title: "haic-libs: Logging and Metrics for Human–AI Collaboration Evaluation"
abstract: >-
  haic-libs is an open-source Python library for evaluating Human–AI
  Collaboration (HAIC) from interaction logs. It consists of two packages:
  haic-logging, which records human and AI decisions into a versioned
  decisions artifact, and haic-metrics, which computes HAIC metrics
  (interaction frequency, action duration, human-centeredness, trust,
  adaptability, effort loss, efficiency, similarity) offline over explicit
  temporal windows and renders Markdown and JSON reports.
